## Exp48 — Position Exit-Clock Orthogonality Test — FROZEN BEFORE SCORE

Scientific question: beyond its already-proven WHICH-SIDE role, does the exact original TRAIN-fitted POSITION_SURV also improve binary EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT prediction relative to BASE_SURV across all eight frozen direction×time environments, without refit, recalibration, Dwell, threshold, alternate Position transform, or new feature?

Frozen target/predictions:

y_exit=1 if observed ADVANCE or RECAPTURE by H; y_exit=0 for NO_EXIT by H.
p_exit_base(H)=1-P_NO_EXIT_BASE(H).
p_exit_pos(H)=1-P_NO_EXIT_POSITION(H).

Reuse exact Exp41 eligible cells at 15/30/60/120m and exact Exp44/45 joint environments. Primary estimand EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED pooled over four horizons. Whole-BRT-day bootstrap preserving all eligible cells by environment/day. Environment must contain EXIT and NO_EXIT and >=2 contributing BRT days, otherwise UNDERPOWERED_EXIT_ENVIRONMENT.

Formal comparison: POSITION_SURV vs BASE_SURV using binary Brier and LogLoss. gain=loss(BASE)-loss(POSITION). Require CI95 lower bound >0 for both metrics in all 8 environments = 16/16.

POSITION_EXIT_CLOCK_TRANSPORT=PASS only at 16/16.
ROBUST_POSITION_EXIT_CLOCK_COMPONENT=PASS only if all environments are scorable and all 16 cells pass.

